Repair the Normalizer for repair-parts grade history. Every input is a real existing-version change and requires two commands in CLOSE,OPEN order. CLOSE must preserve the old grade, surrogate and start; OPEN takes the replacement values. Intervals are half-open, effective is later than prior_from, and all keys are already allocated. The only reported defect is the grade on CLOSE.

Input 0: part string non-null, prior_grade string nullable, next_grade string nullable, prior_sk long non-null, next_sk long non-null, prior_from date non-null, effective date non-null. Output 0: part string non-null, action string non-null, grade string nullable, sk long non-null, from_at date non-null, to_at date nullable. 

```ctl
//#CTL2
function integer count() { return 2; }
function integer transform(integer idx) {
    $out.0.part = $in.0.part;
    if (idx == 0) {
        $out.0.action = "CLOSE";
        $out.0.grade = $in.0.next_grade;
        $out.0.sk = $in.0.prior_sk;
        $out.0.from_at = $in.0.prior_from;
        $out.0.to_at = $in.0.effective;
    } else {
        $out.0.action = "OPEN";
        $out.0.grade = $in.0.next_grade;
        $out.0.sk = $in.0.next_sk;
        $out.0.from_at = $in.0.effective;
        $out.0.to_at = null;
    }
    return ALL;
}
```

Fix first-event classification in this placement-history Reformat. sensor is non-null but the empty string is a legal identity. Events are sorted by sensor then strictly increasing at. First event of each sensor must emit INITIAL even when its location is null or empty. A changed location emits REPLACE with previous location; an unchanged location is dropped. Null location differs from empty. Keep the single-output delta interface.

Input 0: sensor string non-null, location string nullable, at date non-null. Output 0: sensor string non-null, kind string non-null, old_location string nullable, new_location string nullable, at date non-null. 

```ctl
//#CTL2
string lastSensor;
string lastLocation;
function integer transform() {
    boolean initial = lastSensor == null || lastSensor != $in.0.sensor;
    if (!initial && lastLocation == $in.0.location) return SKIP;
    $out.0.sensor = $in.0.sensor;
    $out.0.kind = initial ? "INITIAL" : "REPLACE";
    $out.0.old_location = initial ? null : lastLocation;
    $out.0.new_location = $in.0.location;
    $out.0.at = $in.0.at;
    lastSensor = $in.0.sensor;
    lastLocation = $in.0.location;
    return ALL;
}
```

Repair this Normalizer that creates stock-bin aisle history commands. Input is sorted bin,at, times strictly increasing within bin. An unchanged aisle emits no command and must leave the original version start intact. New bin emits OPEN; changed aisle emits CLOSE then OPEN, preserving previous aisle and start. Null and empty aisle differ. These commands are keyed downstream by bin plus start; half-open intervals.

Input 0: bin string non-null, aisle string nullable, at date non-null. Output 0: bin string non-null, action string non-null, aisle string nullable, start date non-null, end date nullable. 

```ctl
//#CTL2
boolean ready = false;
string bin;
string aisle;
date began;
string[] pendingAisles = [];
date[] pendingStarts = [];
function integer count() {
    clear(pendingAisles);
    clear(pendingStarts);
    boolean continuing = ready && bin == $in.0.bin;
    if (continuing && aisle == $in.0.aisle) { began = $in.0.at; return 0; }
    if (continuing) {
        append(pendingAisles, aisle);
        append(pendingStarts, began);
    }
    append(pendingAisles, $in.0.aisle);
    append(pendingStarts, $in.0.at);
    bin = $in.0.bin;
    aisle = $in.0.aisle;
    began = $in.0.at;
    ready = true;
    return length(pendingAisles);
}
function integer transform(integer idx) {
    boolean opening = idx == length(pendingAisles) - 1;
    $out.0.bin = bin;
    $out.0.action = opening ? "OPEN" : "CLOSE";
    $out.0.aisle = pendingAisles[idx];
    $out.0.start = pendingStarts[idx];
    $out.0.end = opening ? null : $in.0.at;
    return ALL;
}
```

