Fix this hydrology Normalizer downstream of DataIntersection's matched change packets. Every packet represents a real catchment change. Staging needs CLOSE followed by OPEN; CLOSE carries the previous version and OPEN its replacement. Keys are already allocated. Intervals are half-open and effective is later than old_from.

Input GaugeReplacement(gauge:string!,old_sk:long!,next_sk:long!,old_area:string!,new_area:string!,old_from:date!,effective:date!). Output GaugeAction(gauge:string!,op:string!,sk:long!,area:string!,valid_from:date!,valid_to:date?).

```ctl
//#CTL2
function integer count() { return 2; }
function integer transform(integer idx) {
    boolean closing = idx == 1;
    $out.0.gauge = $in.0.gauge;
