The revised payroll attendance segments export follows this priority schedule, with left-to-right posting order.

1 | clock_out equals null | OPEN {minutes=0, segment_from=clock_in plus 0 minutes, segment_to=null, paid=false}
2 | category equals "CANCEL" | empty
3 | duration < 0 | ERROR {minutes=duration, segment_from=clock_in plus 0 minutes, segment_to=clock_in plus duration minutes, paid=false}
4 | not approved | PENDING {minutes=net, segment_from=clock_in plus 0 minutes, segment_to=clock_in plus net minutes, paid=false}
5 | category equals "TRAIN" | TRAIN {minutes=duration, segment_from=clock_in plus 0 minutes, segment_to=clock_in plus duration minutes, paid=false}
6 | category equals "TRAVEL" and duration >= 90 | OUTBOUND {minutes=45, segment_from=clock_in plus 0 minutes, segment_to=clock_in plus 45 minutes, paid=true} -> ONSITE {minutes=duration-90, segment_from=clock_in plus 45 minutes, segment_to=clock_in plus duration-45 minutes, paid=true} -> RETURN {minutes=45, segment_from=clock_in plus duration-45 minutes, segment_to=clock_in plus duration minutes, paid=true}
7 | net > 420 | REGULAR {minutes=420, segment_from=clock_in plus 0 minutes, segment_to=clock_in plus 420 minutes, paid=true} -> OVERTIME {minutes=net-420, segment_from=clock_in plus 420 minutes, segment_to=clock_in plus net minutes, paid=true}
8 | review | WORK {minutes=net, segment_from=clock_in plus 0 minutes, segment_to=clock_in plus net minutes, paid=true} -> AUDIT {minutes=0, segment_from=clock_in plus 0 minutes, segment_to=clock_in plus 0 minutes, paid=false}
9 | otherwise | WORK {minutes=net, segment_from=clock_in plus 0 minutes, segment_to=clock_in plus net minutes, paid=true}

duration is the whole elapsed minutes from clock_in to clock_out; net subtracts break_minutes, treating a missing break as zero. Dates are UTC. Segment boundaries use clock_in plus the listed minute offsets; the segment_to of OPEN is absent. Negative net is allowed only by the explicit ERROR treatment; other complete sheets have break_minutes between zero and duration.

