The revised parcel safety and transport scheduling export follows this priority schedule, with left-to-right posting order.

1 | length_cm <= 0 or width_cm <= 0 or height_cm <= 0 or weight_kg <= 0 | REJECT {endpoint=null, kg=0, due_at=dispatch_at plus 0 elapsed hours, requires_signature=false}
2 | destination equals null | HOLD {endpoint=null, kg=weight_kg, due_at=dispatch_at plus 0 elapsed hours, requires_signature=false}
3 | hazardous | SCREEN {endpoint="HAZMAT", kg=weight_kg, due_at=dispatch_at plus 0 elapsed hours, requires_signature=true} -> HAZMAT {endpoint=destination, kg=weight_kg, due_at=dispatch_at plus 48 elapsed hours, requires_signature=true} -> CERTIFY {endpoint=destination, kg=0, due_at=dispatch_at plus 48 elapsed hours, requires_signature=true}
4 | longest > 120 or weight_kg > 25 | FREIGHT {endpoint=destination, kg=weight_kg, due_at=dispatch_at plus 72 elapsed hours, requires_signature=signature}
5 | dispatch_at >= cutoff_at | empty
6 | review | AUDIT {endpoint=destination, kg=0, due_at=dispatch_at plus 0 elapsed hours, requires_signature=false} -> LINEHAUL {endpoint=destination, kg=weight_kg, due_at=dispatch_at plus 24 elapsed hours, requires_signature=signature}
7 | otherwise | PICKUP {endpoint="LOCAL", kg=weight_kg, due_at=dispatch_at plus 0 elapsed hours, requires_signature=signature} -> DELIVER {endpoint=destination, kg=weight_kg, due_at=dispatch_at plus 48 elapsed hours, requires_signature=signature}

longest is the largest of the three dimensions. A route day means exactly 24 elapsed hours after dispatch_at, including across daylight-saving changes. SCREEN and HAZMAT each describe the same parcel mass, not additive stock movements; CERTIFY and AUDIT carry zero kg. Preserve the requested signature flag except where a rule explicitly forces it.

